WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.963
Step four records a baseline.

2
00:00:01.963 --> 00:00:05.298
The fixtures are two
fictional validation kit runs,

3
00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:08.712
one day apart: October
twenty-eighth and twenty-ninth.

4
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:12.010
Compare the first with
nothing, and it's a baseline:

5
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.825
ten new findings, and
the command exits two.

6
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:17.771
Package it with the
other kits' provenance,

7
00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:21.475
and the evidence manifest's
hash starts six d nine f f f.

8
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:23.663
Step five compares the next day.

9
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:28.407
The summary reads: new three,
resolved one, changed one,

10
00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:33.151
detail only one, unchanged
six, unverified checks two.

11
00:00:33.151 --> 00:00:35.338
Its table shows which checks moved.

12
00:00:35.338 --> 00:00:39.187
VK-CA-01 went from Pass to Fail.

13
00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:42.488
VK-PIV-01 didn't run.

14
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:47.537
And VK-NPI-03 went from Fail to Error.

15
00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:49.038
Look closely at that one.

16
00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:50.875
Yesterday it had a finding.

17
00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:52.363
Today its read failed.

18
00:00:52.363 --> 00:00:55.337
So the finding is
unverified, not resolved.

19
00:00:55.337 --> 00:00:57.580
A failed read is never a fix.
